                    {
                        "sense_id": "6d0f0a36-5ad5-3873-b07e-35207cf4a2b3",
                        "entry_id": "e2fc75d0-4feb-353a-bcde-72c6f8e19df7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "współżycie korzeni lub nasion roślin naczyniowych z grzybami"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ce648bc0-5904-46a3-8c55-eb75f831aaf2",
                                "sense_id": "6d0f0a36-5ad5-3873-b07e-35207cf4a2b3",
                                "text": "Zjawisko mikoryzy dotyczy większości roślin wyższych."
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1.1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9e744cdd-bcce-461e-9ef7-4c59788d1ecb",
                        "source_entry_id": "e2fc75d0-4feb-353a-bcde-72c6f8e19df7",
                        "source_sense_id": "6d0f0a36-5ad5-3873-b07e-35207cf4a2b3",
                        "target_lang_word": "mycorrhiza",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mycorrhiza",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "53fcd931-33ff-32d9-9ff6-f84f8d072aff",
                                        "entry_id": "baf654e8-6cc7-38c8-9321-3e5896e717b3",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A plant root formed in symbiosis with a fungus; the symbiosis between the mycelium of a fungus and the roots of a plant."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4bc4db00-3987-4c30-9b9e-f58fa812541b",
                                                "sense_id": "53fcd931-33ff-32d9-9ff6-f84f8d072aff",
                                                "text": "Alternatively, inoculations of a disturbed site with native or exotic fungi facilitate formation of mycorrhizae in a shorter period, given certain circumstances."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0c608fed-58f7-4d15-8ba5-1eedf3c7e3df",
                                                "sense_id": "53fcd931-33ff-32d9-9ff6-f84f8d072aff",
                                                "text": "This has been associated with advances in different research disciplines such as genetics, genomics, proteomics, metabolomics and physiology, advances which have generated better insight into topics of mycorrhizal biology, including the mechanisms of host-mycorrhiza interactions pre- and post-penetration, the influence of the symbiosis on the host and its surroundings, and the evolution and diversity of mycorrhization."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ce6cfd66-4f76-4fd4-94c1-0ebe2b2b083f",
                                                "sense_id": "53fcd931-33ff-32d9-9ff6-f84f8d072aff",
                                                "text": "In total, mycorrhizae are responsible for helping source the nutrients for about 80 per cent of all modern plant species."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "1729dc60-6efd-406d-b478-6925e6df77dc",
                        "source_entry_id": "e2fc75d0-4feb-353a-bcde-72c6f8e19df7",
                        "source_sense_id": "6d0f0a36-5ad5-3873-b07e-35207cf4a2b3",
                        "target_lang_word": "mycorhize",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "mycorhize",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6bb60e22-3cb5-3d83-a786-97cc9ce3425a",
                                        "entry_id": "01f5253b-82c3-32e6-a425-edf30b4d1974",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Symbiose entre la racine d'une plante et une colonie de champignons, les hyphes de ces derniers (leurs filaments) pénétrant dans la racine."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "209dfb46-8a2e-4f43-b81d-7d99fc76dfbc",
                                                "sense_id": "6bb60e22-3cb5-3d83-a786-97cc9ce3425a",
                                                "text": "En conclusion, il est possible que la clé de la protection des plantes par la mycorhize soit une gestion de l’activité photosynthétique plus efficace."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d1d4c56f-3251-41aa-9631-5089764b6b35",
                                                "sense_id": "6bb60e22-3cb5-3d83-a786-97cc9ce3425a",
                                                "text": "Elaine Gan est aussi l’auteure des illustrations qui séparent les sections des différents chapitres. Elles montrent des spores fongiques, la pluie, des mycorhizes et des champignons."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0f86bf88-ec2d-4128-9d7b-0dfbab0a38e7",
                                                "sense_id": "6bb60e22-3cb5-3d83-a786-97cc9ce3425a",
                                                "text": "Leur mycélium vit en symbiose avec les végétaux (mycorhize) qui, sans leur présence, n’auraient jamais quitté l’océan !"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "mycorhize",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0b28d917-ca74-309d-9e60-6134e6c782d7",
                                        "entry_id": "e93467be-119e-3b2c-b43d-64b22b1543e0",
                                        "glosses": [
